BT 1 0 0 1 0 87.2 Tm /F1 8.8 Tf 12 TL (A firmware flaw in COLDCARD hardware wallets produced predictable \(guessable\) wallet seeds, letting attackers precompute) Tj T* (keys and sweep funds. On 31 Jul ~594 BTC \(~$38M\) was drained from ~500 wallets in a ~25-minute coordinated sweep) Tj T* (\(01:31-01:56 UTC\), with stolen funds consolidated via 1,300+ transfers. Root cause: a March-2021 COLDCARD build setting) Tj T* (instructed the device to skip its own hardware RNG, generating low-entropy seeds instead of secure hardware randomness;) Tj T* -0.04873 Tw (affected are Mk3 devices that generated a seed on firmware 4.0.1+ within the vulnerable window \(~2021-2026\), so the bug was) Tj T* 0 Tw (latent for ~5 years. Weak RNG at seed-generation time is catastrophic and retroactive - funds are drainable years later with no) Tj T* (on-device compromise. Affected Mk3 users must migrate funds to a newly generated seed on patched firmware immediately) Tj T* (and treat any seed created in the vulnerable window as compromised.) Tj T* ET
